From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xu Qianhui <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Subject: [DRAFT PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: bonded broadcast command path for
 SM8750 dual-DSI (B5-P4, Q28 field code)

MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DRAFT for review preparation only (deliver freeze 2026-10-13). Do not
send as-is.

The SM8750 panel is driven over a bonded dual-DSI link (two DSI hosts,
ae94000/ae96000). For command-mode transfers the vendor flow programs
both links into a broadcast pair, arms the master last and waits for
the master completion IRQ. Upstream only implements the simple
need-sync double write, which on this panel intermittently times out
(cold boot ~50%: "command DMA timeout: status=0x2200200", see
Q28 report). This patch carries the vendor bonded path behind the
existing SM8750 selection, plus the enable-timing move
(msm_dsi_host_enable() from bridge pre_enable to bridge enable) that
the vendor flow requires so that the first DCS command sees the link
already in LP11/video-armed state.

Known review concerns (deliberately NOT addressed in this draft):
- The bonded path is reverse-engineered from the vendor drop; several
  magic values (ERR_INT_MASK0 0x001f0200/0x44440400, sw-reset force-on
  clock bits, 200 ms master timeout, 500x10us slave poll) are treated
  as unknown-provenance constants and must be justified before merge.
- Failure policy is "latch and give up" (dsi_bonded_cmd_failed);
  upstream will likely ask for a recoverable error path.
- Depends on the per-SoC config selection work (B5-P1) and the
  controller/PHY per-SoC config (B5-P2); applied here on top of the
  M1 7.3-rc7 payload tree for build verification.

Signed-off-by: Xu Qianhui <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
